{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":489027,"name":"Pat","username":"Pat4","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/p/439d5e/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-11T14:31:07.719Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-489027-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-489027-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-489027-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-489027-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMy Grok Bot on Windows is stuck on the “Can’t reach your computer” screen. Attempting to use the reset tool results in the error: “Reset failed. The reset couldn’t finish. Grok Bot’s computer may be in a partial state.”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-489027-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-489027-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen the Grok Bot desktop application on Windows.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThe app fails to connect and displays the “Can’t reach your computer” screen.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eClick on the “Reset” or “Recover” button to restore the remote agent machine.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThe system attempts to reload, but halts midway and throws the error: “Reset failed. The reset couldn’t finish. Grok Bot’s computer may be in a partial state - retry to run the reset again.”\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eClicking “Retry” indefinitely loops back to the exact same partial state error message.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-489027-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-489027-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen clicking the “Reset” or “Recover” button, the cloud system should completely wipe the broken virtual machine instance, provision a fresh, working agent computer, and automatically re-establish a stable connection to the local desktop app without getting stuck in a half-built or partial loop state.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-489027-operating-system-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-489027-operating-system-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWindows 10/11\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-489027-version-information-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-489027-version-information-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUnknown / App is completely locked on a white screen with a black circle in the middle upon startup, preventing access to the version info panel. Running on the latest Windows Desktop build.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-489027-for-ai-issues-which-model-did-you-use-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-489027-for-ai-issues-which-model-did-you-use-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eFor AI issues: which model did you use?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok 2\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-489027-for-ai-issues-add-request-id-with-privacy-disabled-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-489027-for-ai-issues-add-request-id-with-privacy-disabled-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eFor AI issues: add Request ID with privacy disabled\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003en/a\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-489027-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-9\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-489027-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-9\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYes - Cursor is unusable\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-11T15:24:00.616Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":5,"reads":4,"readers_count":3,"score":25.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":171358,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-windows-computer-stuck-in-partial-state-reset-failed","display_username":"Pat","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":137334,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-windows-computer-stuck-in-partial-state-reset-failed/171358/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":489057,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-11T15:23:25.473Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, thanks for the detailed report. Good news: your Grok Bot cloud computer is fine. It’s working normally, and all your Bots, files, and logins are still there. You don’t need to restore it, so please don’t click Reset or Recover again. Reset isn’t needed here, and when the connection comes back, recovery will try to rebuild something that’s already healthy.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt looks like the Grok Bot app on your Windows PC just can’t reach our servers. It connected fine before, so something likely changed on the PC or on its network. The app connects directly and does not use Windows system proxy settings, so security software, a proxy, or a VPN can block it even if the browser works normally. That also explains the stuck loading screen and the failed resets. The app is waiting for a connection it never gets.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTry these steps in order:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFully quit Grok Bot: right click the tray icon bottom right near the clock, then click Quit. Reopen it and wait 2 minutes.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCheck security software: antivirus with HTTPS scanning or web protection, a corporate proxy, or a VPN. Temporarily disable that feature or add Grok Bot to exceptions, then quit and reopen the app.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIn Windows: Settings \u0026gt; Network \u0026amp; internet \u0026gt; Proxy. If a proxy is enabled, turn it off or add an exception. Also try with VPN turned off.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eInstall the latest Grok Bot version over your current one from \u003ca href=\"http://cursor.com/download\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003eCursor · Download\u003c/a\u003e. You’re on 0.30.0, which is a couple weeks old. Newer builds show clearer connection errors. Your Bots are stored on the cloud computer, so reinstalling won’t lose anything.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eNetwork test: connect your PC to a mobile hotspot, quit and reopen Grok Bot, then wait 2 minutes. If it works on hotspot but not on your normal network, something on that network or on the PC security setup is blocking it.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf nothing helps, tell me which step you got stuck on, and paste the lines containing \u003ccode\u003e[unavailable]\u003c/code\u003e or \u003ccode\u003e[internal]\u003c/code\u003e from \u003ccode\u003e%APPDATA%\\Grok Bot\\desktop-structured-log-spill.v1.json\u003c/code\u003e. Let me know how it goes.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-11T15:23:25.473Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":5.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":171358,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-windows-computer-stuck-in-partial-state-reset-failed","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"http://cursor.com/download","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Cursor · Download","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":750,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-windows-computer-stuck-in-partial-state-reset-failed/171358/5","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":489201,"name":"Pat","username":"Pat4","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/p/439d5e/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:59:21.845Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThank you so much! It was Kaspersky.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":7,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-11T18:59:21.845Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":5,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":2,"readers_count":1,"score":0.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":171358,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-windows-computer-stuck-in-partial-state-reset-failed","display_username":"Pat","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post"